xmodel/sol-probabilities-0821.md:19:**Estimate: 5% by 2031-08-21 (a five-year horizon).** I count success only as an expert-checkable characteristic-zero proof of JC2 or an explicit characteristic-zero polynomial Keller counterexample. “Current avenues” means the named programs in this snapshot and their direct technical descendants—sheet-book/FC closure, the D43/D75/H29 residue-A experiments, PCC/WTC/log-ramification, Euler-characteristic/nonproperness, DC2, and the off-axis/formal-construction work—pursued at roughly comparable intensity; I exclude a conceptually unrelated future breakthrough merely adopted by the campaign. The positive case is genuine: repeated computational cliffs have yielded small exact certificates, D25 gives 576 disjoint affine 14-cells at each tested prime, and the radical-fiber symmetry is proved. But D25 survived rather than died, no germ was certified in the sampled cells, D23 and D25 used the same depth window, and D43 is only the first new operator measurement while still consuming conjectural x-side and registry inputs. The proof routes lack a complete global landing or absolute degree bound; the counterexample route must still cross modular-to-formal, characteristic-zero, algebraization, globalization, and polynomiality gaps. Calibrationally, I assign about 6% campaign success conditional on JC2 being true and about 1% conditional on it being false; using the 70/30 truth split gives 4.5%, rounded to 5%.
